# The EverBetter tool catalog.
#
# One entry per tool a design may name. An entry is a DECISION, not an inventory
# row: the rationale is the part that stops the research being redone.
#
# Entries are read by the design validator, by preflight, and by the interview —
# which uses them to ask "use this, or is your process different?" instead of
# asking a person to do research.

@catalog
owner: Buzz, process owner
reviewed: 2026-10-05
source_of_truth: maxwell-k8s/charts for existence; this file for policy

@tool eb-appointment-service
provides: appointment_id, patient_ref, clinician, starts_at, duration_minutes, status
via: tools/eb-appointment-service
data_class: phi
may_not: leave the local boundary
chosen: 2026-09, over polling FHIR directly
because: already deployed, and carries clinician and status in one call
decided_by: Buzz, process owner
review_by: 2027-09

@tool eb-form-builder-service
provides: submission_id, patient_ref, form, submitted_at, flagged
via: tools/eb-form-builder-service
data_class: phi
may_not: leave the local boundary
chosen: 2026-09, over a bespoke intake form
because: clinicians already author forms in it; submissions carry a flag the triage rule needs
decided_by: Buzz, process owner
review_by: 2027-09

@tool keychain
provides: secret
via: security
data_class: credential
may_not: be written to a file or passed as a command-line argument
chosen: 2026-10, over a dotenv file
because: survives a reboot, is not readable by a stray process listing, and is macOS native
decided_by: Buzz, process owner
review_by: 2027-10

@tool local-ledger
provides: append-only rows
via: sqlite3
data_class: operational
may_not: hold PHI in clear text
chosen: 2026-10
because: no server, durable, queryable by anything
decided_by: Buzz, process owner
review_by: 2027-10
